s@gmail.com\"},{\"name\":\"bnoordhuis\",\"email\":\"info@bnoordhuis.nl\"},{\"name\":\"es128\",\"email\":\"elan.shanker+npm@gmail.com\"},{\"name\":\"paulmillr\",\"email\":\"paul@paulmillr.com\"},{\"name\":\"pipobscure\",\"email\":\"pip@pipobscure.com\"}],\"contributors\":[{\"name\":\"Philipp Dunkel\",\"email\":\"pip@pipobscure.com\"},{\"name\":\"Ben Noordhuis\",\"email\":\"info@bnoordhuis.nl\"},{\"name\":\"Elan Shankar\",\"email\":\"elan.shanker@gmail.com\"},{\"name\":\"Miroslav Bajtoš\",\"email\":\"mbajtoss@gmail.com\"}],\"homepage\":\"https://github.com/fsevents/fsevents\",\"bugs\":{\"url\":\"https://github.com/fsevents/fsevents/issues\"},\"os\":[\"darwin\"],\"dist\":{\"shasum\":\"49ffb097c132987fc84938f5e97c3a6632e04c13\",\"tarball\":\"https://registry.npmjs.org/fsevents/-/fsevents-2.0.3.tgz\",\"fileCount\":19,\"integrity\":\"sha512-kbyPVQrgcnetW389rufw+WAl9szz0ougHcW6faFZ/RDESUwgmCWnzmXHONmdKSWiadtj6VaaewwhyX7ckL+itw==\",\"signatures\":[{\"sig\":\"MEQCIHRLLQkqI6qK6wP2IXLZlzKgJdJrnAn5nE0DIBcqJh8sAiBFqgNWnYBfs5HQrqnCplN/X6r/RdejeH08ZMFSY2HShg==\",\"keyid\":\"SHA256:jl3bwswu80PjjokCgh0o2w5c2U4LhQAE57gj9cz1kzA\"}],\"unpackedSize\":57191,\"npm-signature\":\"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\r\\nVersion: OpenPGP.js v3.0.4\\r\\nComment: https://openpgpjs.org\\r\\n\\r\\nwsFcBAEBCAAQBQJcohdICRA9TVsSAnZWagAA/X4QAJXf5B6Hgd7GMc7v/C5Z\\n4MkBwheeh2UqxRut5Yk8eV1wBxYJOv6aIe29wXnU8ZAdZnuyv+BzvlExz+eB\\n9tOGcitO9UH+IXwiBibZnVf/wfYmbBpqXYmW44rBMcmmi/XkDBF/0W5FzXjq\\nAOpmLK/I5Ru1NP1Ry3ruJGwAxzj7T9VUatQM5OUQvnHylvCMaCo2TqMDj9iZ\\nw0tXNKJGNG3DJPqPO3jGR9QgrfF7JZ3GgTb951BvpqQwUUdcYMEhEXNLz8ct\\n4ZPul/znwhy4/igmUcis6fUPje5RX/4mGhuaE4m2rgE8Nem484kZdLbABTRE\\nXXA08BVuy2Q4DkybgCoZH7KnKpyjjlDdrrFTkPntHcePk2KfX9xMtzGURrc5\\nEL2BE+mHlI4QTC+v07PPTOxvQ2f+Yzk8mDDMZVd1pz1MYcOF/nR1BA5ihUXp\\nuLKqGoVi2Edjroq62rtTNKZ9hBC8sjXipXjFMd76ki3bkUJutBKEWyUtKb//\\nd7iACLGmIcL6vmFopJM3N0t2q4EifSkScQaAdgh9R4Rmwbo2xR4BC60pasBD\\nhrnRiM9itQfGOSLMt2xGSZvlG7vG+zuX7WbFoDk8NSqbKKgjfhHHxMl8M9P8\\nsZwUUQgIg7MXYudoVkVANYYUwm43Izgt7/dk30iP0JjJa76fvv2MRBXQdfoS\\nLBGF\\r\\n=uR6L\\r\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\r\\n\"},\"main\":\"fsevents.js\",\"readme\":\"# fsevents [![NPM](https://nodei.co/npm/fsevents.png)](https://nodei.co/npm/fsevents/)\\n\\nNative access to MacOS FSEvents in [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/)\\n\\nThe FSEvents API in MacOS allows applications to register for notifications of\\nchanges to a given directory tree. It is a very fast and lightweight alternative\\nto kqueue.\\n\\nThis is a low-level library. For a cross-platform file watching module that\\nuses fsevents, check out [Chokidar](https://github.com/paulmillr/chokidar).\\n\\n## Installation\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm install fsevents\\n```\\n\\n## Usage\\n\\n```js\\nconst fsevents = require('fsevents');\\nconst stop = fsevents.watch(__dirname, (path, flags, id) => {\\n  const info = fsevents.getInfo(path, flags, id);\\n}); // To start observation\\nstop(); // To end observation\\n```\\n\\nThe callback passed as the second parameter to `.watch` get's called whenever the operating system detects a\\na change in the file system. It takes three arguments:\\n\\n`(path: String, flags: Number, id: String) => {}`\\n\\n * `path` - the item in the filesystem that have been changed\\n * `flags` - a numeric value describing what the change was\\n * `id` - an unique-id identifying this specific event\\n\\n###### `fsevents.getInfo(path, flags, id): FsEventInfo => {}`\\n\\nThe `getInfo` function takes the `path`, `flags` and `id` arguments and converts those parameters into a structure\\nthat is easier to digest to determine what the change was.\\n\\nThe `FsEventsInfo` has the following shape:\\n\\n```js\\n/**\\n * @typedef {'created'|'modified'|'deleted'|'moved'|'root-changed'|'unknown'} FsEventsEvent\\n * @typedef {'file'|'directory'|'symlink'} FsEventsType\\n */\\n{\\n  \\\"event\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"file.txt\\\", // {FsEventsEvent}\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"file\\\",    // {FsEventsType}\\n  \\\"changes\\\": {\\n    \\\"inode\\\": true,   // Had iNode Meta-Information changed\\n    \\\"finder\\\": false, // Had Finder Meta-Data changed\\n    \\\"access\\\": false, // Had access permissions changed\\n    \\\"xattrs\\\": false  // Had xAttributes changed\\n  },\\n  \\\"flags\\\": 0x100000000\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## License\\n\\nThe MIT License Copyright (C) 2010-2018 by Philipp Dunkel, Ben Noordhuis, Elan Shankar — see LICENSE file.\\n\\nVisit our [GitHub page](https://github.com/fsevents/fsevents) and [NPM Page](https://npmjs.org/package/fsevents)\\n\",\"engines\":{\"node\":\"^8.16.0 || ^10.6.0 || >=11.0.0\"},\"gitHead\":\"e6d9e603d76422656570615ffa27728bee8f2fe0\",\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"/bin/bash ./test.sh 2>/dev/null\",\"clean\":\"node-gyp clean && rm -f fsevents.node\",\"install\":\"[ -f fsevents.node ] || npm run prepublishOnly\",\"prepublishOnly\":\"node-gyp clean && rm -f fsevents.node && node-gyp rebuild && node-gyp clean\"},\"_npmUser\":{\"name\":\"pipobscure\",\"email\":\"pip@pipobscure.com\"},\"repository\":{\"url\":\"git+https://github.com/fsevents/fsevents.git\",\"type\":\"git\"},\"_npmVersion\":\"6.7.0\",\"description\":\"Native Access to Mac OS-X FSEvents\",\"directories\":{},\"_nodeVersion\":\"11.13.0\",\"_hasShrinkwrap\":false,\"readmeFilename\":\"README.md\",\"devDependencies\":{},\"_npmOperationalInternal\":{\"tmp\":\"tmp/fsevents_2.0.3_1554126663037_0.09363294808882094\",\"host\":\"s3://npm-registry-packages\"}},\"2.0.4\":{\"name\":\"fsevents\",\"version\":\"2.0.4\",\"keywords\":[\"fsevents\",\"mac\"],\"license\":\"MIT\",\"_id\":\"fsevents@2.0.4\",\"maintainers\":[{\"name\":\"bajtos\",\"email\":\"mbajtoss@gmail.com\"},{\"name\":\"bnoordhuis\",\"email\":\"info@bnoordhuis.nl\"},{\"name\":\"es128\",\"email\":\"elan.shanker+npm@gmail.com\"},{\"name\":\"paulmillr\",\"email\":\"paul@paulmillr.com\"},{\"name\":\"pipobscure\",\"email\":\"pip@pipobscure.com\"}],\"contributors\":[{\"name\":\"Philipp Dunkel\",\"email\":\"pip@pipobscure.com\"},{\"name\":\"Ben Noordhuis\",\"